{"id":"torrey:medo-persian-kingdom","source":"torrey","name":"Medo-Persian Kingdom","slug":"medo-persian-kingdom","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Extended from India to Ethiopia — Es 1:1.","refs":[["Esth",1,1,1,1]]},{"text":"Peopled by descendants of Eliam — Ge 10:22.","refs":[["Gen",10,22,10,22]]},{"text":"Silver part of image in Nebuchadnezzar’s dream. — Da 2:32,39.","refs":[["Dan",2,32,2,32],["Dan",2,39,2,39]]},{"text":"A bear. — Da 7:5.","refs":[["Dan",7,5,7,5]]},{"text":"A ram with two horns. — Da 8:3,20.","refs":[["Dan",8,3,8,3],["Dan",8,20,8,20]]},{"text":"Shushan a chief city of — Es 1:2; 8:15.","refs":[["Esth",1,2,1,2],["Esth",8,15,8,15]]},{"text":"Achmetha or Ecbatana a chief city of — Ezr 6:2.","refs":[["Ezra",6,2,6,2]]},{"text":"Divided into many provinces — Es 1:1; Da 6:1.","refs":[["Esth",1,1,1,1],["Dan",6,1,6,1]]},{"text":"Laws of, unalterable — Da 6:12,15.","refs":[["Dan",6,12,6,12],["Dan",6,15,6,15]]},{"text":"Ruled by, absolute kings — Es 3:8,11; 7:9.","refs":[["Esth",3,8,3,8],["Esth",3,11,3,11],["Esth",7,9,7,9]]},{"text":"Cyrus. — Ezr 1:1.","refs":[["Ezra",1,1,1,1]]},{"text":"Ahasuerus or Cambyses. — Ezr 4:6.","refs":[["Ezra",4,6,4,6]]},{"text":"Artaxerxes Smerdis (an usurper). — Ezr 4:7.","refs":[["Ezra",4,7,4,7]]},{"text":"Darius Hystaspes. — Ezr 6:1; Da 5:31.","refs":[["Ezra",6,1,6,1],["Dan",5,31,5,31]]},{"text":"Xerxes. — Da 11:2.","refs":[["Dan",11,2,11,2]]},{"text":"Artaxerxes Longimanus or Ahasuerus. — Ezr 6:14; 7:1; Es 1:1.","refs":[["Ezra",6,14,6,14],["Ezra",7,1,7,1],["Esth",1,1,1,1]]},{"text":"Called kings of Assyria. — Ezr 6:22.","refs":[["Ezra",6,22,6,22]]},{"text":"Called kings of Babylon. — Ne 13:6.","refs":[["Neh",13,6,13,6]]},{"text":"Styled themselves king of kings. — Ezr 7:12.","refs":[["Ezra",7,12,7,12]]},{"text":"Dwelt in royal palaces. — Es 1:2; 8:14.","refs":[["Esth",1,2,1,2],["Esth",8,14,8,14]]},{"text":"Were exceeding rich. — Es 1:4; Da 12:2.","refs":[["Esth",1,4,1,4],["Dan",12,2,12,2]]},{"text":"Entertained magnificently. — Es 1:3,5,7.","refs":[["Esth",1,3,1,3],["Esth",1,5,1,5],["Esth",1,7,1,7]]},{"text":"Held in their hand a golden sceptre. — Es 5:2.","refs":[["Esth",5,2,5,2]]},{"text":"Put to death all who approached them without permission. — Es 4:11,16.","refs":[["Esth",4,11,4,11],["Esth",4,16,4,16]]},{"text":"Celebrated for wise men — Es 1:13; Mt 2:1.","refs":[["Esth",1,13,1,13],["Matt",2,1,2,1]]},{"text":"People of, warlike — Eze 27:10; 38:5.","refs":[["Ezek",27,10,27,10],["Ezek",38,5,38,5]]},{"text":"Peculiar customs in — Es 1:8; 2:12,13.","refs":[["Esth",1,8,1,8],["Esth",2,12,2,12],["Esth",2,13,2,13]]},{"text":"Babylon taken by the king of — Da 5:20,31.","refs":[["Dan",5,20,5,20],["Dan",5,31,5,31]]},{"text":"The Jews delivered from captivity by means of — 2Ch 36:20,22,23; Ezr 1:1-4.","refs":[["2Chr",36,20,36,20],["2Chr",36,22,36,22],["2Chr",36,23,36,23],["Ezra",1,1,1,4]]},{"text":"Extensive conquest. — Da 8:4.","refs":[["Dan",8,4,8,4]]},{"text":"Conquest of Babylon. — Isa 21:1,2; Da 5:28.","refs":[["Isa",21,1,21,1],["Isa",21,2,21,2],["Dan",5,28,5,28]]},{"text":"Deliverance of the Jews. — Isa 44:28; 45:1-4.","refs":[["Isa",44,28,44,28],["Isa",45,1,45,4]]},{"text":"Invasion of Greece under Xerxes. — Da 11:2.","refs":[["Dan",11,2,11,2]]},{"text":"Downfall by Alexander. — Da 8:6,7; 11:3.","refs":[["Dan",8,6,8,6],["Dan",8,7,8,7],["Dan",11,3,11,3]]}],"refCount":62}
